7.	Clothing, Equipment, etc., on Proceeding
on Spring or Harvest Leave:
Where a soldier is granted spring or harvest leave under the provisions of this Order, he will be permitted to take with him necessary clothing and uniform. Except when specially authorized otherwise by the G.O.C.-in-C. or D.O.C. concerned, he will only be authorized to wear his uniform while travelling to the place where he will reside during leave and while returning from such place on the expiration of his leave. The cost of making good any deficiency in clothing or equipment issued to the soldier, as shown on his M.F.C. 800, before proceeding on leave, or found to he deficient upon his return from leave, will be recovered in the usual manner.
8.	Furlough Form to be Furnished Soldier on
Proceeding on Spring or Harvest Leave:
Before proceeding on leave the soldier will be given Furlough Form M.F.B. 322, with those portions of instructions on reverse side thereof which deal with dress and medical attention while on leave, struck out and initialled by the officer authorized to issue same. The soldier will be given explicit instructions in writing from his officer commanding which will include:-
(a)	Conditions governing wearing of uniform;
(b)	Cessation of pay and allowances;
(c)	His being subject to recall at any time on 48 hours' notice;
(d)	His non-entitlement to dental and medical care during leave;
(e)	When and to whom, and how to apply if extension of leave required;
(f)	When, where, and to whom to report on expiration of leave required;
(g)	The necessity of obtaining his commanding officer's permission (under C.A.R.O. 2242) to marry to be eligible for dependents' allowance on return from leave.
9.	Medical Examination of Soldier Proceeding
on Spring or Harvest Leave:
As the period of spring or harvest leave authorized does not exceed sixty days, no medical examination will be necessary before proceeding on such leave. Should a soldier die or be killed while on leave, either during or as a direct result of his employment, but not otherwise, he will be entitled to a military funeral as a soldier, in accordance with Article 220, F.R. & I. (Canada).
